From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fernando Silva da Luz <51529517+FernandoSLuz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: power_wrap: write the DVFSRC flag only on N1x
 laptops

power_wrap writes the DVFSRC enable flag into SPM SYSRAM on every
system whose NVDA6210 device reports PLID 2 (MT8901). The flag and its
address come from the N1x laptops' Windows PEP driver, but the GB10
desktops report the same platform id and get the write too. A DMI
match already skips it on the NVIDIA DGX Spark; the other
GB10 systems still get it.

On an ASUS Ascent GX10 (DMI "ASUSTeK COMPUTER INC." / "GX10", BIOS
GX10DGX.0106.2026.0707.0731) with the write active, the machine reset
or reported kernel memory corruption within 13-36 minutes at idle in
7 of 7 boots. With power_wrap kept from probing
(initcall_blacklist=power_wrap_init) and everything else unchanged,
it ran 12 h 41 min clean, idle and under load. With this patch on
7.3-6 the driver logs "DVFSRC: not an N1x laptop, leaving firmware
policy unchanged" and still writes BestPerf, with all LPI states
enabled.

Write the flag only on the N1x laptops, told apart from the GB10
desktops by their MediaTek I2C controllers (NVDA0200), as the USB4
release default already does. This replaces the DGX Spark DMI match
and covers every GB10 system without a per-product list. BestPerf and
the rest of power_wrap are unchanged.

The firmware mechanism behind the resets is still unknown.

Signed-off-by: Fernando Silva da Luz <51529517+FernandoSLuz@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/power_wrap/power_wrap.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/power_wrap/power_wrap.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/power_wrap/power_wrap.c
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/power_wrap/power_wrap.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/power_wrap/power_wrap.c
@@ -3,7 +3,6 @@
  * Copyright (c) 2026 MediaTek Inc.
  */
 #include <linux/acpi.h>
-#include <linux/dmi.h>
 #include <linux/init.h>
 #include <linux/io.h>
 #include <linux/miscdevice.h>
@@ -595,6 +594,16 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The N1x laptops' I2C controllers (NVDA0200) set them apart from the GB10
+ * desktops (DGX Spark, ASUS Ascent GX10 and the other GB10 systems), which
+ * report the same MT8901 platform id.
+ */
+static bool pwrap_is_n1x_laptop(void)
+{
+	return acpi_dev_present("NVDA0200", NULL, -1);
+}
+
 /**
  * pwrap_write_dvfsrc_flag() - Enable DVFSRC via the SPM SYSRAM flag
  * @dev: device (used for logging)
@@ -615,10 +624,13 @@
 {
 	void __iomem *vaddr;
 
-	/* The DGX Spark resets at idle when this firmware flag is set. */
-	if (dmi_match(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "NVIDIA") &&
-	    dmi_match(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "NVIDIA_DGX_Spark")) {
-		dev_info(dev, "DVFSRC: leaving firmware policy unchanged on DGX Spark\n");
+	/*
+	 * The flag comes from the N1x laptops' Windows PEP driver. The GB10
+	 * desktops reset at idle when it is set, so leave their firmware
+	 * policy unchanged.
+	 */
+	if (!pwrap_is_n1x_laptop()) {
+		dev_info(dev, "DVFSRC: not an N1x laptop, leaving firmware policy unchanged\n");
 		return;
 	}
 
@@ -833,13 +845,9 @@
 	unsigned int i;
 	int ret;
 
-	/*
-	 * The N1x laptops' I2C controllers (NVDA0200) set them apart from the
-	 * GB10 desktops, which report the same platform id.
-	 */
 	if (!usb4_release_set &&
 	    IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_USB4_PLATFORM_NHI) &&
-	    acpi_dev_present("NVDA0200", NULL, -1))
+	    pwrap_is_n1x_laptop())
 		usb4_release = false;
 
 	if (!usb4_release) {
